0001 | """Champion Agent V15.5: Recovery-Window Selling (V15 + price-gated surplus front-loading).
0002 | 
0003 | Built from the kevin park forensics (Δ−1876) and the other 4 real V15 losses:
0004 | 
0005 | Root cause found: V15's tape dumps STRAWBERRY/MILK at fixed late steps that land in
0006 | CRASHED markets (px 1-24 at steps 599/615/666/717), while winning opponents sell
0007 | surplus into PRICE RECOVERY windows (px 68@598, 32@614, 53@647, 47@665, 85@715,
0008 | 62@716) that appear as town shops drain inventory between dumps. The opponent's
0009 | 12+12+1 STR @ 715/716/717 vs V15's 24 @ 717 alone explains ~1,188 of the kevin
0010 | delta; summing all mid-game windows fully accounts for the 2,223 STR revenue gap.
0011 | 
0012 | Second defect: V15's _terminal_liquidation APPENDS STR at market-queue position 3
0013 | (after MILK/WOOL/WHEAT), so it sells AFTER the glut; the opponent FRONT-LOADS STR
0014 | at position 0. In the lockstep engine, position order is execution order, so
0015 | front-loaded surplus sells quote against pre-glut inventory.
0016 | 
0017 | V15.5 = V15 + _recovery_sell pass:
0018 | - From step 570 (day 24) through 715 (day-29 recovery), when the CURRENT market
0019 |   price of STRAWBERRY/MILK/WOOL is >= gate, sell up to 12 units of shed surplus
0020 |   (beyond the tape's planned sells) at the FRONT of the market queue.
0021 | - Everything else (capselllate, preempt, rank_sell_slots, terminal liquidation)
0022 |   is unchanged from V15.
0023 | 
0024 | Empirically verified: pending diag_bench H2H vs kaggle_boat84_v14 / kaggle_champion_v15.
0025 | """
